content.text:
Now garage CSS. Insert after `.card-foot span` before `.menu-bottom` maybe. We'll write comprehensive.

Garage screen:
```
#screen-garage {
  display: grid; grid-template-rows: auto 1fr auto;
  padding: 26px 42px 24px;
  background:
    linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(6,7,9,.92) 0%, rgba(6,7,9,.35) 30%, rgba(6,7,9,.12) 60%, rgba(6,7,9,.86) 100%),
    radial-gradient(...)
}
```
Need car visible. Background gradient top and bottom. Left copy maybe small and overlay near left top of stage, but car center. Text "YOUR CAR. YOUR COLOUR." could be at top-left below header. It might overlap car if car left, but car is centered. At 1280, car length from x~300 to x~800. Left copy width 330 from x 42 to ~372 would overlap car nose. Hmm. The screenshot car nose at x~370. So copy could overlay slightly. Maybe place stage copy top-left with narrow width 270 and car centered; slight overlap acceptable? Better: center car and put copy in upper-left only h2 small (50px) and paragraph under, could still. Alternatively put copy bottom-left above dock? The dock starts at bottom. Maybe skip large copy and just a vertical label along left: "LIVERY STUDIO" monospace, plus headline partially behind car is fine, similar to menu where card overlays car. The menu intentionally layers text over car. So okay.

Let's set garage-stage position relative, copy absolute left 0 top 4vh max-width 360, h2 60px. Live paint chip absolute right 0 top? Right side is free (no card). Car centered; live chip top-right good.

Dock: width 100%, max maybe 1080? A full-width bar at bottom with glass. padding 18px 22px. body grid 1fr auto; presets and custom. Height ~200. On 1280, swatches 14 across at 34px + gaps = 14*34 + 13*8 = 580, fits. Custom ~500. Body grid columns 1fr 1fr maybe.

Structure:
```
.garage-dock { position: relative; z-index: 3; width: 100%; padding: 16px 22px 12px; }
.garage-dock-head { display flex; justify-content space-between; padding-bottom 10; border-bottom}
.garage-dock-body { display:grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1.1fr) minmax(0,1fr); gap:24; padding:14px 0 10px;}
.garage-presets > .mono, .garage-custom > .mono { display block; color dim-2; font-size 8; margin-bottom 9}
.garage-swatches { display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(14, minmax(0,1fr)); gap:7px; }
.garage-swatch { position:relative; aspect-ratio:1; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14); border-radius:50%; background: var(--swatch); transition...; }
.garage-swatch::after { content:''; ... inset? check indicator }
.garage-swatch span { position:absolute; inset:3px; border-radius:50%; border:2px solid transparent; }
.garage-swatch.is-active { border-color: var(--cream); box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px rgba(243,239,229,.18), 0 0 18px var(--swatch); transform: translateY(-2px) }
.garage-swatch.is-active span { border-color: rgba(0,0,0,.32); }
.garage-custom-row { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:10px; flex-wrap:wrap;}
.garage-wheel { position:relative; display:inline-flex; cursor:pointer; }
.garage-wheel input { position:absolute; opacity:0; width:1px; height:1px; pointer-events:none; }
.garage-wheel-ui { display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:9px; padding:10px 14px; border:1px solid var(--line); background: rgba(255,255,255,.025); font-family: font-display; ... clip path maybe }
.garage-wheel-ui i { width:18px; height:18px; border-radius:50%; background: conic-gradient(...); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.3); display:block; }
```
Color wheel input styled: clicking label triggers native color picker; `input[type=color]` hidden but label click should open. Note: hidden with opacity 0 and size 1x1 might still open when label clicked. Usually yes. Better input absolute inset 0 opacity 0 width 100% height100% cursor pointer, appended over label. But then input is invisible and clicking entire label opens picker. Do:
```
.garage-wheel { position:relative; display:inline-flex; }
.garage-wheel input { position:absolute; inset:0; width:100%; height:100%; opacity:0; cursor:pointer; }
```
Then label text behind. Good, click works.

Hex form:
```
.garage-hex { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:6px; border:1px solid var(--line); background: rgba(7,9,12,.7); padding: 3px 4px 3px 10px; }
.garage-hex label { color dim-2; font-size 7.5 }
.garage-hash { color: var(--orange); font-family mono; font-size 11 }
.garage-hex input { width: 84px; background:none; border:0; color: var(--cream); font: 600 12px var(--font-mono); letter-spacing:.12em; text-transform:uppercase; outline:none; }
.garage-hex input.is-invalid { color: var(--bad); }
.garage-hex .btn-sm { padding: 7px 11px; min-height: 30px; min-width: 0; font-size: 10px; }
.garage-reset { margin-left:auto; }
.garage-dock-foot { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; border-top:1px solid var(--line-soft); padding-top:9px; color: var(--dim-2); font-size:7px; }
.garage-live { position:absolute; right:0; top: 2vh; display:flex... background glass; padding; border; }
.garage-live-dot { width:26px;height:26px;border-radius:50%;}
```
Need hide garage stage copy on smaller screens.

Garage header: height 70, flex.

Mobile responsive at max 900:
- screen padding 14px 16px
- garage header title hide
- stage copy h2 36px, maybe hide paragraph
- live chip top right
- dock padding 12, body single column, swatches repeat(7). Dock might be too tall. At 390x844: header 58, stage ~? dock 300, car visible 480. Fine.
- On mobile, garage stage copy could be top-left with h2 40. Live chip below maybe. Could hide copy entirely to keep car visible. Let's keep h2 hidden on <=760? User needs car. We can hide stage copy paragraph and h2 become 30px at top-left. Dock 260. Let's estimate. Fine.

Add `.garage-screen` to `@media (max-width: 900px)` etc.

Also `.garage-screen` background gradient must not fully hide WebGL. Use rgba.

Let's write CSS insertion before `.menu-bottom`.

