content.text:
Now responsive CSS. Add at max 1180 garage padding maybe 24 30, dock body gap. At 900, adjust. Let's add to existing media queries.

At max 1180:
```
.garage-dock-body { gap: 22px; }
#screen-garage { padding: 22px 30px 18px; }
```
At 900:
```
#screen-garage { padding: 14px 16px 14px; }
.garage-header { height: 44px; }
.garage-header-title { display:none; }
.garage-stage-copy { top: 2vh; max-width: 240px; }
.garage-stage-copy h2 { font-size: 34px; margin: 10px 0 8px;}
.garage-stage-copy p { display:none; }
.garage-live { top: auto; bottom: 1vh; } hmm could overlap dock? Stage area shrinks.
.garage-dock-body { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 14px; padding: 12px 0 10px; }
.garage-swatches { grid-template-columns: repeat(7, minmax(0,1fr)); gap:8px; }
.garage-dock-foot { display:none; }
.garage-custom-row { gap: 8px; }
```
At 760:
```
.garage-stage-copy h2 { font-size: 30px; }
.garage-live { padding: 8px 10px; }
.garage-live-name { display:none; }
.garage-live strong { font-size: 16px; }
.garage-reset { margin-left: 0; }
.garage-dock { padding: 12px 14px 10px; }
```
At 440 maybe swatches repeat(7) still.

Also #screen-garage background may hide car more on mobile. Fine.

Add to respective blocks.

